  "corrections": [
    {
      "source_file": "host/hardware-prep.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-304229bc33260b9d",
      "start": 21,
      "end": 21,
      "before": "For verification, the self-test preflight enforces the current minimum thresholds (CUDA support, reliability gate, direct ports, PCIe bandwidth, internet bandwidth, VRAM, system RAM). The canonical list lives in [Verification Stages: requirements](/host/verification-stages#additional-requirements-for-verification).",
      "after": "By default, self-test preflight checks CUDA support, reliability, direct ports, PCIe bandwidth, internet bandwidth, VRAM, and system RAM before launching a test instance. `--ignore-requirements` can bypass failed requirement checks for diagnosis; it does not establish verification eligibility. See [Verification Stages: requirements](/host/verification-stages#additional-requirements-for-verification).",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/hardware-prep.mdx",
        "start": 21,
        "end": 21
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/hardware-prep.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-e028f1d157aa8857",
      "start": 53,
      "end": 53,
      "before": "Do not blindly copy old Ubuntu 22.04 cgroup-v1 workaround commands onto Ubuntu 24.04. Docker, kernel, and cgroup defaults differ by OS version; follow the current Vast host installer path for the OS you are actually using, and treat cgroup errors as install diagnostics to fix before listing.",
      "after": "Do not blindly copy old Ubuntu 22.04 cgroup-v1 workaround commands onto Ubuntu 24.04. Check the running host’s cgroup version and Docker configuration, use the current Vast host installer for that OS, and investigate cgroup errors before listing. A workaround for one configuration may not apply to another.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/hardware-prep.mdx",
        "start": 53,
        "end": 53
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-2e9855b2bfd1629b",
      "start": 45,
      "end": 49,
      "before": "```bash\necho -n \"40000-40799\" | sudo tee /var/lib/vastai_kaalia/host_port_range\nsudo systemctl restart vastai.service\nsudo tail -n 50 /var/lib/vastai_kaalia/kaalia.log | grep host_port_range\n```",
      "after": "```bash\n# Apply network changes during planned maintenance after reviewing active rentals.\nprintf %s \"40000-40799\" | sudo tee /var/lib/vastai_kaalia/host_port_range &&\nsudo cat /var/lib/vastai_kaalia/host_port_range &&\nsudo systemctl restart vastai.service\n# Inspect daemon output separately for startup or network errors.\nsudo tail -n 50 /var/lib/vastai_kaalia/kaalia.log\n```",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
        "start": 45,
        "end": 52
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-f7c51d576b0bd26d",
      "start": 51,
      "end": 51,
      "before": "The log should show `host_port_range: 40000 40799`.",
      "after": "Confirm that the stored range is `40000-40799` and matches your router/firewall rules. Check daemon logs for errors after the restart, then test reachability from outside the LAN; reading back the file does not prove that forwarding works.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
        "start": 54,
        "end": 54
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-fc60d0d32545eabe",
      "start": 56,
      "end": 56,
      "before": "Vast instances need public inbound TCP and UDP reachability. CGNAT, double NAT without a real public forwarding path, many residential Starlink setups, incompatible IPv6-only service, blocked inbound ports, or no public inbound IP are not supported for hosting because renters and self-test must be able to reach the machine directly.",
      "after": "Vast hosting requires a public IPv4 address with inbound TCP and UDP forwarding for the configured direct-port range. CGNAT and shared ISP addresses are not supported by the published setup requirements. With double NAT or an IPv6-only service, establish a working public IPv4 forwarding path before listing; an outbound internet connection alone is insufficient.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
        "start": 59,
        "end": 59
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-353ec73533415d0c",
      "start": 121,
      "end": 121,
      "before": "Self-test timeouts and `Port Networking Issues` usually mean a network-path problem. [`vericode=8`](/host/glossary#vericode) means a host-facing machine error is present; use the exact visible message to confirm whether it is the port-networking case. See [Self-Test Reference: vericode=8](/host/self-test-reference#vericode-8) and [no response for 120s](/host/self-test-reference#no-response-120s).",
      "after": "`Port Networking Issues` indicates that the platform’s inbound port-reachability check could not connect. A self-test timeout can also involve a missing progress server, a crashed container, or a stalled test; inspect the reported stage and logs. [`vericode=8`](/host/glossary#vericode) means a host-facing machine error is present; use the exact visible message to identify the cause. See [Self-Test Reference: vericode=8](/host/self-test-reference#vericode-8) and [no response for 120s](/host/self-test-reference#no-response-120s).",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/network-ports.mdx",
        "start": 124,
        "end": 124
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-5fe002872d48998d",
      "start": 29,
      "end": 29,
      "before": "The command can include an account-specific machine installation key. Do not reuse commands from old notes, shell history, screenshots, third-party guides, or another account. A regular API key is not a setup-page installation key.",
      "after": "The command can include account-specific authorization material for machine installation. Copy it from the current setup page for the intended account. Do not reuse old commands or substitute a different account’s credential. Do not assume a separately configured API key is an interchangeable substitute; obtain the current command from Setup for the intended account.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 29,
        "end": 29
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-b3fe73c46ed288bb",
      "start": 58,
      "end": 58,
      "before": "If the wizard stops at NVIDIA/CUDA checks, repair the driver, reboot, confirm `nvidia-smi` shows every GPU, then rerun the wizard.",
      "after": "If the wizard stops at NVIDIA/CUDA checks, inspect the reported failure and confirm that the driver supports the installed GPUs and required CUDA runtime. Repair the driver if needed, reboot if the driver change requires it, and confirm `nvidia-smi` sees the expected GPUs before rerunning the wizard.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 58,
        "end": 58
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-a4798d2b43f36535",
      "start": 72,
      "end": 83,
      "before": "```bash\nmkdir -p ~/vast-install\ncd ~/vast-install\nwget https://console.vast.ai/install -O install\nread -rsp \"Paste fresh Vast host setup key: \" VAST_HOST_KEY\necho\nsudo python3 ./install \"$VAST_HOST_KEY\" \\\n  --no-driver \\\n  --docker-partition /dev/mapper/vg1-lv--1 \\\n  --ports 40000 40799\nunset VAST_HOST_KEY\n```",
      "after": "```bash\nmkdir -p ~/vast-install &&\ncd ~/vast-install &&\nwget https://console.vast.ai/install -O install &&\nIFS= read -r -s -p \"Paste current Vast host setup key: \" VAST_HOST_KEY &&\nprintf '\\n' &&\n[ -n \"$VAST_HOST_KEY\" ] &&\nsudo python3 ./install \"$VAST_HOST_KEY\" \\\n  --no-driver \\\n  --docker-partition /dev/mapper/vg1-lv--1 \\\n  --ports 40000 40799\nunset VAST_HOST_KEY\n```",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 72,
        "end": 84
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-a867339d8abea496",
      "start": 103,
      "end": 103,
      "before": "Refresh the setup page, copy a fresh command, confirm host account access, and rerun the wizard. Use the wizard error, installer log, and daemon logs to decide what to fix.",
      "after": "Use the wizard error, installer log, and daemon logs to identify and address the failed check. Confirm the intended host account, refresh the setup page and copy its current command before retrying the wizard.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 104,
        "end": 104
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-77d6739f1372753a",
      "start": 108,
      "end": 108,
      "before": "If the installer or daemon logs show an HTTP 4xx while registering or identifying the machine, work through these causes in order:",
      "after": "If the installer or daemon logs show an HTTP 4xx while registering or identifying the machine, retain the response and check the following possible causes:",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 109,
        "end": 109
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-826ddc7e60bc7a49",
      "start": 110,
      "end": 110,
      "before": "1. **Truncated or mangled setup key.** Always copy the full command with the setup page's copy button; a partial paste fails authentication. Get a fresh command and rerun.",
      "after": "1. **Truncated or mangled setup command.** Use the setup page’s copy button to obtain the complete current command for the intended account. Check for a partial paste or unintended edits before retrying; use the actual response to investigate any remaining authentication error.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 111,
        "end": 111
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-ff12f9da3f0ab4ab",
      "start": 112,
      "end": 112,
      "before": "3. **Account not converted to a host account.** The API rejects machines from client-only accounts. See [Host Account and Agreement](/host/account-hosting-agreement#agreement-stuck).",
      "after": "3. **Account hosting setup incomplete.** Confirm that you selected the intended host account and completed its hosting agreement flow. See [Host Account and Agreement](/host/account-hosting-agreement#agreement-stuck).",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/installing-host-software.mdx",
        "start": 113,
        "end": 113
      }
    },
    {
      "source_file": "host/first-24-hours.mdx",
      "id": "MCL-85ad73e07ddbb88f",
      "start": 80,
      "end": 80,
      "before": "Verification, search visibility, and first rentals are not instant. Passing self-test makes the machine eligible; timing still depends on machine health, supply, demand, and platform policy.",
      "after": "Passing self-test is a readiness check; it does not by itself guarantee verification, search placement, or rentals. Verification is automated and has no fixed timeline. Keep the machine healthy and online, and distinguish platform verification from whether renters choose the offer.",
      "after_span": {
        "source_file": "host/first-24-hours.mdx",
        "start": 80,
        "end": 80
      }
    }
